
Import Tokens
 Top  Previous  Next  
 

For custom imports, there is a token that maps to each PHDWin field that can be imported. The following section describes each import token you will see. The tokens are listed by the section in which they appear in the program's Import Center: Case Titles, Columnar Production, Daily Production, Economics, Misc Dates, Other, Price/Expense, Prod Volumes, Test Data and Wellbore Completion.

hmtoggle_plus1 Case Titles



API County Code
 
Maps non-hyphenated alphanumeric value to "API Number" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Expects 3 characters. Use with "API State Code" and "API Well Code". Do not use with "Well API Code". Will create and populate Test Data Zone/well for multi-well cases Multi "Well API Code" values imported to one case.  Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

API State Code
 
Maps non-hyphenated alphanumeric value to "API Number" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Expects 2 characters. Use with "API County Code" and "API Well Code". Do not use with "Well API Code". Will create and populate Test Data Zone/well for multi-well cases Multi "Well API Code" values imported to one case.  Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

API Well Code
 
Maps non-hyphenated alphanumeric value to "API Number" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Expects 5 or more characters. Use with "API State Code" and "API County Code". Do not use with "Well API Code". Will create and populate Test Data Zone/well for multi-well cases Multi "Well API Code" values imported to one case. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Case API Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "API Number" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab ONLY. Maximum of 40 characters. Do not use with "API State Code", "API County Code" or "API Well Code". Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Case Memo
 
Maps to the case memo field.  Existing case memos will be overwritten.
 

Case Multiplier
 
Multiplication factor used for risking cases that is applied to the entire case. The case is run under normal conditions, and then all of the reported numbers are multiplied by this factor for output.
 

Case Name
 
Maps alphanumeric value to Case Name field or UWI field (for Canadian cases) of the Case Editor. Maximum 40 characters. Only one name or UWI supported per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Country
 
Maps alphanumeric value to Country of the Case Editor. Maximum of 30 characters. Only one country name per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

County
 
Maps alphanumeric value to County of the Case Editor. Also used for Parish in Louisiana or Pool in Canada. Maximum of 30 characters. Only one county name per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Field Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Field Code" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Maximum of 40 characters. Will contain Stage Field codes from commercial data vendors. Only one county name per case.  Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Field Name
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Field" of the Case Editor. Maximum of 40 characters. Only one Field name per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Gas Gatherer
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Gas Gatherer" of the Production Test Tab of the Case Editor. Maximum of 25 characters. Only one Gas Gatherer name per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Gas Gravity
 
Maps numeric value to Gas Specific Gravity (Reference Air) in the Production Test tab of the Case Editor. Supports values > 1.0. One allowed per case. Multiple values not supported; last value imported will be used. No support for importing to Reservoir Fluids Tests. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Latitude
 
Maps numeric value to Latitude field of the Case Editor's General Info tab. Supports positive and negative values to 8 decimal places. No support for Min. or Sec. One allowed per case. Last one imported per case is saved. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Location
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Location" field of the Case Editor's General Info tab. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Longitude
 
Maps numeric value to Longitude field of the Case Editor's General Info tab.  Supports positive and negative values to 8 decimal places. No support for Min. or Sec. One allowed per case. Last one imported per case is saved. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Major Phase
 
Maps to and sets a case's major phase. Supports "Oil" or "Gas" only. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Offshore
 
Offshore/Onshore switch
 

Oil Gatherer
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Oil Gatherer" of the Production Test Tab of the Case Editor. Maximum of 25 characters. Only one Oil Gatherer name per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Oil Gravity
 
Maps numeric value to "Oil Gravity" in the Production Tests tab of the Case Editor and sets the gravity units to Specific Gravity. Can be viewed on the Case Editor's Expense tab.  Supports values > 1.0.
 

Operator Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Operator Code" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Maximum 40 characters. Only one Operator Code per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries.  Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Operator Name
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Operator Name" field of the Case Editor. Maximum of 30 characters. Only one Operator Code per case. Use "User-Defined ID Code" for alternate entries.  Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Partnership
 
Designates a partnership for newly created investments or changes in ownership.  If this token is not used, then the currently active partnership will receive the results of the import.
 

Primary Import ID Code
 
This is a special import token that is used to associate all remaining data in a given record to one specific case. This token will automatically map to the first data element per record of any data to be imported. The data element must identify a case's unique alphanumeric value as prompted for during the initial import set up. It can only be mapped once per table or sheet.
 

PRMS Category
 
Petroleum Resources Management System: Used to classify cases and indicate the degree of certainty that the resources will be extracted. The category falls under the case's class. Examples of PRMS category include proved, probable, possible, etc. 
 

PRMS Class
 
Used to classify cases. Examples of PRMS class include reserves, contingent, prospective, etc.
 

PRMS Subcategory
 
Used to classify cases and fall below the case’s category. Subcategories include producing, non-producing, shut-in, behind pipe, etc.
 

Res Category (Class & Cat Abbr)
 
Maps Reserve Category abbreviations to the reserve category. The following abbreviations are converted: DP (Producing), BP (Behind Pipe), NP (Non-Producing), SI (Shut-In), UD (Undeveloped). Does not convert: PA (P&A) or IJ (Injection)
 

Res Pressure
 
Maps one Reservoir Pressure per test point. Requires "Test Date-Start Record" OR "Well Number-Start Test" w/ "Test Date" or "Well Number-Start Test-No Append" w/ "Test Date" on same line. Units are defined by existing case convention for existing cases or default import unit convention for new cases.
 

Res Temp
 
Maps one Casing Pressure per test point. Requires "Test Date-Start Record" OR "Well Number-Start Test" w/ "Test Date" or "Well Number-Start Test-No Append" w/"Test Date" on same line. Units are defined by existing case convention for existing cases or default import unit convention for new cases.
 

Reservoir
 
Imports an alphanumeric string into the Reservoir field. Supports up to 40 characters.
 

Retrieval Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Retrieval Code" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Maximum of 40 characters. Do not map for Aries import. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only
 

RRC District Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "RRC Dist Code" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Maximum of 40 characters. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only
 

State
 
Imports a two character state, parish or province. (e.g. TX, Al, NM)
 

Temp Gradient (deg/100ft or deg/100m)
 
Imports the average temperature increase per 100 ft or 100 M. Units are defined by case's existing Unit Convention or default convention is used if new case is created. No unit conversions are applied.
 

Temp Gradient (deg/ft or deg/m)
 
Imports the average temperature increase per ft or M. Units are defined by case's existing Unit Convention or default convention is used if new case is created. No unit conversions are applied.
 

Total Depth
 
Imports a single numerical value per case. Case units or default convention for new wells is used. No unit conversions are applied.
 

Tubing Diameter
 
Imports the inside diameter of a tubing string. Only one per case supported. Case units or default conventions for new cases are used. No unit conversions are applied.
 

Unit Convention
 
Defines import convention and thus units for incoming data for a case. Conventions can change case by case. Alphanumeric. Must match existing convention in PHDWin. If no match, "Imperial" convention assumed. Highly recommended all incoming data conforms to one Unit Convention. OR  Must be consistent for entire incoming data set for a single case.
 

User-Def Gravity (cur product)
 
Measure of  relative density for current product
 

User-Def Gravity Current Product
 
Measure of  relative density for current product
 

User-Def Gravity Type (cur product)
 
Acceptable values are "API", "SG", or "Gas"
 

User-Defined ID Code
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "Operator Code" field of the Case Editor's ID Code tab. Maximum of 40 characters. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.  Case-level Static Variable values can also be imported using this token.  This token will not import Global-level static variables, nor will it create new static variables.
 

UWI Code (Canada)
 
Maps alphanumeric value to "UWI Code" field of the Case Editor's General Info tab for Canadian cases ONLY. Used in Canada instead of Case Name. Requires "Primary Import ID Code".
 

Volume Multiplier
 
Multiplication factor used to risk a case. It is applied to the volumes of the case before economics are run. This method of risk affects mostly revenues and volumes, and only those expenses that are tied to production volumes.
 

Well Num- Append to Case Name
 
Used to map test data or wellbore/completion data to the correct wellbore in the case.  This text will be appended to the Case Name of a case.  This is the import trigger token for production tests and for wellbore/completion data
 

Well Num- No Append to Case Name
 
Used to map test data or wellbore/completion data to the correct wellbore in the case.  This text will be not appended to the Case Name of a case.  This is the import trigger token for production tests and for wellbore/completion data
 

Well Spacing
 
Imports a numerical value for the spacing description for a case.  Maximum of 6 characters.  Used with case's existing Unit Convention.  New cases will use the default convention.
 

Well Type
 
Imports the Well Type listed in the Gen Info tab of the Case Editor.  Values must match existing types in the Case Editor, or the Well Type will list as "Unknown."  Types include Flowing, Pump, Inject, Unknown, SWD, & Source.
 

