Creates a single segment, case specific NGL % volume shrinkage. Overwrites existing shrinkage. Units in % shrink and supports 9 decimal places. Cannot be used with "NGL Shrink (fixed)". No support for multi-segment shrinkage import. Trying to import multiple segments will result in only last segment being used. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

NGL Shrink (fixed)
 
Creates a single segment, case specific NGL fixed volume shrinkage and is the volume per month shrunk in base units as defined by the case. Overwrites existing shrinkage; if multiple segments are imported, only last value is used. No unit conversions are calculated. Supports negative and positive values to 12 digits (combined, including all digits and decimal.) Cannot be used with "NGL Shrink (%)". Overwrites all existing shrink. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

NGL Shrink (frac)
 
Creates a single segment, case specific NGL % volume shrinkage. Units are fractional and represent remaining volume. A 0.94 value represents a 6% shrinkage. Converted to % shrinkage. Overwrites any existing shrink. Supports 9 decimal places. Cannot be used with "NGL Shrink (Fixed)" or "NGL Shrink (%)". No support for multi-segment shrinkage import. Import of multiple Shrink (%) per case not compounded, rather last value used. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Oil Cum Prior Hist
 
Imports known oil cums prior to monthly historical input.
 

Oil Production [Prod Date]
 
Must be preceded by "Production Date" token. Monthly numeric oil volume will be populated for the production month specified. Units are expected to be in base units of the convention used to import the data. i.e. MBbl, E3M3, etc.
 

Oil Shrink (%)
 
Creates a single segment, case specific Oil % volume shrinkage. Overwrites existing shrinkage. Units in % shrink and supports 9 decimal places. Cannot be used with "Oil Shrink (fixed)". No support for multi-segment shrinkage import. Trying to import multiple segments will result in only last segment being used. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Oil Shrink (fixed)
 
Creates a single segment, case specific Oil fixed volume shrinkage and is the volume per month shrunk in base units as defined by the case. Overwrites existing shrinkage; if multiple segments are imported, only last value is used. No unit conversions are calculated. Supports negative and positive values to 12 digits (combined, including all digits and decimal.) Cannot be used with "Oil Shrink (%)". Overwrites all existing shrink. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Oil Shrink (frac)
 
Creates a single segment, case specific Oil % volume shrinkage. Units are fractional and represent remaining volume. A 0.94 value represents a 6% shrinkage. Converted to % shrinkage. Overwrites any existing shrink. Supports 9 decimal places. Cannot be used with "Oil Shrink (Fixed)" or "Oil Shrink (%)". No support for multi-segment shrinkage import. Import of multiple Shrink (%) per case not compounded, rather last value used. Requires "Primary Import ID Code" only.
 

Prod year (yyyy)- Start Record
 
Specifies the year for columnar production.  Used in conjunction with "______ Production (month)" tokens.
 

Production Date
 
This is the date for importing production data in conjunction with tokens that list [Prod Date].  This date should be in format mm/dd/yyyy (or the corresponding non-US format) and the days (dd) should be listed as 1 for the first day of the month because production with this token is monthly.
 

User-Defined Product [Prod Date]
 
Must be preceded by "Production Date" token. Monthly numeric user defined (as defined by the field name) volume will be populated for the production month specified.  Units are expected to be in base units of the convention used to import the data. i.e. MBbl, E3M3, etc.  PHDWin will match on the import fields name to define the product.
 

Water Cum Prior Hist
 
Imports known water cums prior to monthly historical input.
 

Water Inj [Prod Date]
 
Must be preceded by "Production Date" token. Monthly numeric water injection volume will be populated for the production month specified. Units are expected to be in base units of the convention used to import the data. i.e. bbl, etc.
 

Water Production [Prod Date]
 
Must be preceded by "Production Date" token. Monthly numeric water volume will be populated for the production month specified. Units are expected to be in base units of the convention used to import the data. i.e. bbl, etc.
 

Well Count [Prod Date]
 
Must be preceded by "Production Date" token. Monthly numeric well count number will be populated for the production month specified.
 

